{"sessionId":"01a12099-1975-72e1-8865-813c03710022","update":{"_meta":{"piToolCallId":"call_950f0195cb8f448db8e16417"},"kind":"other","locations":[],"rawInput":{"plan":"# Plan: Add `hello()` to greeting.py\n\n## Goal\nCreate `greeting.py` containing a `hello()` function that returns the string `\"Hello, world!\"`.\n\n## Constraints\n- Single file: `greeting.py` in the working directory root.\n- No external dependencies.\n- Function is importable and returns the greeting string (does not print).\n\n## Chunks\n\n### Chunk 1 — Create greeting.py with hello()\n- **Scope**: New file `/var/folders/sl/j50k6cnn5h1_f4sz6ktrtlw80000gn/T/kimchi-live-acp-work-jzveFP/greeting.py` defining `def hello() -> str: return \"Hello, world!\"`.\n- **Files Changed**: `greeting.py` (created).\n- **Depends On**: None.\n- **Accept When**:\n  1. `python -c \"import greeting; print(greeting.hello())\"` prints `Hello, world!`.\n  2. `hello()` returns (not prints) the string `\"Hello, world!\"`.\n- **Test Coverage**: Verified via the one-line import check above; no test file warranted for a single trivial function.\n- **Open Questions**: None.\n\n## Verification Strategy\nRun `python3 -c \"import greeting; assert greeting.hello() == 'Hello, world!'; print('OK')\"` and confirm `OK` is printed.\n\n## Decision Log\n- `hello()` returns the string rather than printing it — standard for library-style functions and easier to test. Rejected: printing inside the function.\n- No test file created — a one-line runtime check is sufficient for a function this small.\n\n## Risks\n- None material. Directory is empty, so no existing code can conflict."},"status":"pending","title":"submit_plan","toolCallId":"kt.submit_plan.2","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update"}}
